------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream dataset
------------------------------------------------------------------------

LOCUS is built on the arXiv split of the Local Citation Recommendation
dataset of Gu, Gao and Hahnloser (ECIR 2022), doi:10.1007/978-3-030-99736-6_19.
That dataset is theirs and is governed by their terms; obtain it from them.

No upstream text is redistributed by this project. The released artefact
bundle carries paper and context IDENTIFIERS, integers and booleans only.
Titles, abstracts and citation windows appear nowhere in it. This is
directly checkable for the bundle's `.jsonl` rows -- each is line-oriented
JSON whose string fields are identifiers -- and holds for the rest of the
bundle too: `locus_manifest_{split}.json` and `bundle_manifest.json` add
only descriptive prose about the release itself (never upstream text), and
`cocitation_train.npz`'s only string array (`vocab`) holds identifier
strings, with every other array holding counts or indices.

The released bundle (identifiers and derived counts) is licensed
CC-BY-4.0. The code is Apache-2.0.

